          "final_text_tail": "s canonical dicts with the `tool_calls` key.\n   - Parses valid JSON strings before normalization, and preserves invalid / non-JSON strings as-is.\n\n2. **Task 2: Deterministic Parse Fingerprinting for `ToolCalls`**\n   - Added `canonicalize_args` to recursively sort dict keys, convert tuples to lists, and strip leading/trailing whitespace on string values without coercing numeric or boolean types.\n   - Added `compute_tool_call_fingerprint` to serialize `{\"name\": name, \"args\": canonical_args}` with `json.dumps(..., sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))` and hash it using SHA-256.\n   - Added `fingerprint: str` (64-char hex) and `id: str` (first 8 hex chars) fields to [`ToolCalls.ToolCall`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-yw83omu2/repo/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py#L283), computed once at creation time in `__init__` and enforced as read-only.\n   - Works seamlessly when creating `ToolCalls` via [`ToolCalls.from_dict_list`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-yw83omu2/repo/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py#L318) or direct validation.\n\n3. **Testing**\n   - Added unit tests covering all flexible parsing scenarios, input validation returns, stable fingerprinting, whitespace trimming, tuple normalization, and read-only attribute constraints in [tests/adapters/test_tool.py](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-yw83omu2/repo/tests/adapters/test_tool.py). All tests pass.\n",
